WEBVTT

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.125
"Letter of Acceptance" "Examinee No.: 64" "Name: Nagisa Shiota"

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:15.833
"Letter of Acceptance" "Examinee No.: 64" "Name: Nagisa Shiota"
I got in!

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:19.292
I'm finally past the worst of it...

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:22.792
You all got in to one of your top two schools!

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:24.583
Congratulations!

00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:27.500
Splendid job wielding those
second blades of yours!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.500
You'll all move on to high school
like the twinkling stars you are!

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.875
It's a weight off my shoulders, too!

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:37.292
"Hooray! You Made It!!" "Congratulations!"
We were supposed to start our final career counseling...

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:40.375
"Hooray! You Made It!!" "Congratulations!"
...but first there's something I'd really like to do.

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:40.792
"Tentacle"
...but first there's something I'd really like to do.

00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:42.583
"Tentacle"
And what does one do,

00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.625
on such a joyous occasion?

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.167
Editing.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.417
What for?!

00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:53.792
I'm making a yearbook,
of course--just for the E Class!

00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:01.833
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:04.833
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.292
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:10.125
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:12.667
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.375
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:20.625
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:26.708
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:31.250
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:37.375
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:41.958
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.500
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.500
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.625
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:54.167
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:58.250
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.250
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.750
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.208
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:08.833
"8 Days Till Koro Sensei's Dead-Line"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:11.333
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:14.167
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:27.958
"21st Period: Trust Time"
"by Koki Mimura"

00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:30.542
Making a yearbook?

00:02:30.542 --> 00:02:31.375
Yes!

00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:35.458
Oh, right--we did a whole-school one.

00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:37.792
With Mr. Karasuma as our teacher.

00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:42.042
And poor Koro Sensei isn't in a single shot.

00:02:42.042 --> 00:02:43.167
Actually...

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:46.833
...he popped into a few
at Mach speed, just under the radar.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.875
It's like one of those ghost photos.

00:02:48.875 --> 00:02:53.375
Exactly! That's why I want to use
<i>these </i>photos instead!

00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:55.792
A year of unguarded moments!

00:02:55.792 --> 00:02:58.292
These treasured selfies with all of you--

00:02:58.292 --> 00:02:59.750
thirty thousand in all!

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.042
Now to find the most
memorable ones together!

00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:04.500
When did you take all these?!

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.583
That's our peeping Sensei.

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:10.125
I don't really like
looking at pictures of myself.

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:11.125
Why not?

00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:12.583
My eyes are so tiny.

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:14.375
Don't worry--

00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:17.667
"Hunk" "Twofer!!" "BTF: Best Teacher Forever"
I've made versions with the "big-eye" filter, too.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.167
"Hunk" "Twofer!!" "BTF: Best Teacher Forever"
How terribly kind of you.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.792
The official yearbook does have
plenty of the usual shots...

00:03:23.792 --> 00:03:27.250
If we're making another one,
we can be more unconventional!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.000
Leave it to me!

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.125
Cool beauty Hayami at the pet shop...

00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:36.125
Oh! And here's a nighttime
campus shot of Mimura on air guitar!

00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:38.792
H-He was behind us all along?

00:03:38.792 --> 00:03:40.917
I'm just getting started!

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:44.500
Princess Kataoka,
trying on her royal vestments!

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.000
Dainty Muramatsu,
right when a cockroach scurried out!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Naked Okajima, running around
the grounds at night in the buff!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.667
Whoa, hang on!

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:57.792
So there could be some
super sketchy pics of me in there?!

00:03:57.792 --> 00:04:00.583
Sketchier than <i>that</i>?

00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:03.500
Find your own photos, all of them!
Then get rid of them!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.417
Oh, my! Who knew editing
would get you so fired up?

00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:09.125
"A Classic Fail!!"

00:04:09.292 --> 00:04:10.875
"How Much For This?"

00:04:11.042 --> 00:04:13.083
"Cheaters Never Win!!"

00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:14.833
"A Dead Ringer!"

00:04:15.042 --> 00:04:16.583
"Who's Doing the Inviting Now?"

00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:18.500
"Play Dress-Up in Moderation..." "Maid Outfit"

00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:23.333
I can't believe he took pictures of <i>that</i>...

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:26.625
Okay, next we'll choose photos
for our school events!

00:04:26.625 --> 00:04:27.542
"Killing It at Exams!!"
How about these? Huh? What do you think?

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:28.625
"Killing It at Summer Vacation!!"
How about these? Huh? What do you think?

00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:29.583
"Killing It at the School Festival!!"
How about these? Huh? What do you think?

00:04:30.458 --> 00:04:34.958
This really was a one-of-a-kind year...

00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:38.042
Oh, but I haven't taken <i>nearly </i>enough photos!

00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:40.500
I was aiming for
a ten-thousand-page yearbook!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.333
And we just keep tearing them up.

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:45.167
The dictionary's not even
three thousand pages!

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:46.583
Outside, class!

00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:49.708
We'll dress up and get a wider variety of shots!

00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:51.375
"Theme: Bio-History"
That's it!

00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:51.875
"Theme: Japanese History" "Divine Retribution"

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:53.208
"Theme: Japanese History" "Divine Retribution"
That's the way...

00:04:53.208 --> 00:04:53.625
"Theme: History of Religion"

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.542
"Theme: History of Religion"
Yes, nice!

00:04:55.542 --> 00:04:58.500
Keep going! More outfits!

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.208
Koro Sensei helped us a lot
with our entrance exams this February,

00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:05.917
but otherwise it's just been a free-for-all.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:09.292
Yeah, with us totally at his mercy.

00:05:09.292 --> 00:05:12.167
He's probably spoiling you.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:16.625
You've come plenty far,
thanks to your classes through January.

00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:21.792
--Hey, babe--Karma got away from me. Lend me a hand, you two.
--Now he wants to spoil his full-fledged students a little.

00:05:21.792 --> 00:05:23.542
I bet that's what he's thinking.

00:05:23.542 --> 00:05:24.583
Oh, I get it.

00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:29.625
Do <i>you </i>think we turned out
like that, too, Mr. Karasuma?

00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:31.000
Sure.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.833
If I ever have a hard time,
I'd trust you without hesitation.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.125
I can count on you.

00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:42.000
A man and a woman, in April...
Living together, in April...

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.458
In April...

00:05:43.458 --> 00:05:45.750
Ten times a day!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.375
What's with all the mumbling lately?

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:50.958
Maybe she found religion.

00:05:54.292 --> 00:05:56.333
What's the meaning of this?

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:59.458
We need to get you in on
the cosplay action, Mr. Karasuma.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:02.042
Or is this a fitting?

00:06:02.042 --> 00:06:04.417
Karasuma, I can't <i>wait </i>for that first night.

00:06:04.417 --> 00:06:06.042
Shut your mouth!

00:06:06.042 --> 00:06:11.208
Phew! That ought to be
enough on-campus photos.

00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:12.375
Hang on a sec!

00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:15.417
Then why are we all stuffed in this bag?!

00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:18.125
On-campus photos are hardly sufficient.

00:06:18.125 --> 00:06:20.833
I'll be taking photos
with you around the world!

00:06:20.833 --> 00:06:21.750
What, <i>now</i>?!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:22.708
You're kidding!

00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:24.500
Why go to such lengths?!

00:06:25.542 --> 00:06:28.750
Because it's fun. And that's also why

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.542
I'll take the time and effort
to use my ingenuity

00:06:30.542 --> 00:06:32.958
and tackle the yearbook with all my might!

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:35.042
Here we go!

00:06:35.042 --> 00:06:37.250
Gum-Gum...

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.292
...Slingshot!

00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:59.667
So I just need to pass this test?

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:03.792
Yep. You have what it takes
to go back to school with confidence.

00:07:03.792 --> 00:07:08.667
Heck, you can breeze
right through the first term's work.

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:11.708
You can use that time
to get used to your new class.

00:07:11.708 --> 00:07:13.292
Yeah...

00:07:14.958 --> 00:07:17.833
When this is done, I'll go back to school.

00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:20.708
When this is done, I'll go back to school.

00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:22.292
When this is done...

00:07:22.292 --> 00:07:22.750
...I'll go...

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.208
"Garbage" "Go home!" "Dummy" "Gross"
...I'll go...

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:26.583
...back to...

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.000
My blade...

00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:43.500
...is most powerful
when used in an assassination.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.125
But...

00:07:45.125 --> 00:07:47.208
Nagisa?

00:07:47.208 --> 00:07:50.375
It's all right; calm down.

00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:52.958
You can do it if you try.

00:07:52.958 --> 00:07:55.542
I know you can.

00:07:55.542 --> 00:07:57.833
I will!

00:07:57.833 --> 00:08:00.375
It's a different way of using my blade,

00:08:00.375 --> 00:08:02.250
but if I get to see that look on her face...

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.083
"Final Career Counseling Sessions"
"Once you're done, go on home!"

00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.708
Now, then...

00:08:06.708 --> 00:08:11.250
Have you found what you'd like to be, Nagisa?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.292
Koro Sensei...

00:08:15.292 --> 00:08:18.417
I'm going to be a teacher.

00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:21.708
I'm not fast like you,

00:08:21.708 --> 00:08:24.708
or invincible like you,

00:08:24.708 --> 00:08:28.167
or smart like you...

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:32.583
But I want to be a teacher like you.

00:08:33.875 --> 00:08:37.958
That's good. It suits you.

00:08:37.958 --> 00:08:40.250
You each have a talent
bestowed on you all equally

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.750
that you will also lose equally someday:

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.250
youth.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.125
Keep swimming forward now, without stopping,

00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:52.458
before this talent, your youth, escapes you.

00:08:52.458 --> 00:08:53.875
Yes, sir!

00:08:54.292 --> 00:08:54.708
"Staff Room"

00:08:54.708 --> 00:08:56.583
"Staff Room"
See you tomorrow, Koro Sensei!

00:08:56.583 --> 00:08:59.250
"Staff Room"
Yes, see you then.

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:06.167
Is that it for the career counseling?

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:10.667
Yes. They really impress me, all of them.

00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:14.250
The only big task left is editing that yearbook.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:17.208
Looks like I'll be spending
my nights here for a while.

00:09:17.208 --> 00:09:18.083
I see.

00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:20.417
I'll need an article about the developments

00:09:20.417 --> 00:09:21.958
in your relationship with Ms. Irina.

00:09:21.958 --> 00:09:24.500
I'll be spending the next
five hours interviewing you.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.625
Like hell! I'm leaving!

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.167
Make it an educational yearbook.

00:09:40.708 --> 00:09:47.875
I have to admit, we've learned
so much in this classroom you've built.

00:09:47.875 --> 00:09:50.083
Both the students...

00:09:50.083 --> 00:09:51.583
...and me.

00:09:56.292 --> 00:09:58.083
Report.

00:09:58.083 --> 00:09:59.292
--He's in a classroom alone right now.

00:09:59.292 --> 00:10:01.417
--But how do I choose?
--He's in a classroom alone right now.

00:10:01.417 --> 00:10:04.042
He won't be moving anytime soon.

00:10:04.042 --> 00:10:06.500
Well done, Special Agent Karasuma.

00:10:07.292 --> 00:10:09.625
You heard the man.

00:10:09.625 --> 00:10:13.625
Tonight, March 6, just as planned...

00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:16.708
...we move forward with our final assassination.

00:11:06.958 --> 00:11:10.958
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.458
The first shot is a direct hit
on the entire school building!

00:11:19.458 --> 00:11:20.292
And the target?

00:11:20.292 --> 00:11:21.833
Checking the footage now!

00:11:21.833 --> 00:11:26.000
Look at that--not a single scratch
anywhere in the place.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.500
That's our Anti-Tentacle-Creature
Permeable Laser Satellite:

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.708
a.k.a. "Spear of Heaven."

00:11:31.708 --> 00:11:35.750
Modeled after a tortoise
and powered by antimatter lifeforms,

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.708
then further amplified
in a gigantic particle accelerator,

00:11:38.708 --> 00:11:41.750
it fires a laser from
an altitude of 400 kilometers.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:45.000
This laser passes through any and all obstacles,

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.250
liquefying only tentacle creatures.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:51.042
And we've just fired it
without one bit of advance warning.

00:11:51.042 --> 00:11:53.417
Surely that did the trick.

00:11:57.625 --> 00:12:02.083
The roof and my clothing are fine--
it's just my tentacles!

00:12:03.167 --> 00:12:04.375
My goodness.

00:12:04.375 --> 00:12:07.292
Impossible... He dodged that?!

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:08.792
But it's a light-speed laser!

00:12:08.792 --> 00:12:11.417
What canny intuition.

00:12:11.417 --> 00:12:14.958
But it's not over yet.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.458
Since you're alive and all,

00:12:18.458 --> 00:12:21.542
why don't you try
running away, super-creature?

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:29.542
There's another weapon waiting for you there.

00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:49.042
Our Anti-Tentacle-Creature
Permeable Laser Barrier:

00:12:49.042 --> 00:12:52.167
a.k.a. "Shield of Earth."

00:12:52.167 --> 00:12:54.250
A cluster of camouflaged ground facilities

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.708
converging lasers to form a barrier

00:12:57.708 --> 00:12:59.917
that covers the entire mountain.

00:13:02.333 --> 00:13:04.458
Is this...

00:13:06.833 --> 00:13:09.042
He's got nowhere to run!

00:13:09.042 --> 00:13:11.875
The lasers penetrate into the ground,

00:13:11.875 --> 00:13:16.458
a cage of light--not to kill him,
but to prevent his escape.

00:13:16.458 --> 00:13:19.250
I wanted to finish him off with that first shot.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:24.208
Once Plan B is in motion,
all hell will break loose.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:26.083
Ready the ground troops!

00:13:26.083 --> 00:13:28.083
Emergency deployment per Case B-1!

00:13:28.083 --> 00:13:29.500
Sir!

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.417
What the--

00:13:32.417 --> 00:13:34.375
What's that light?

00:13:35.417 --> 00:13:37.875
We were naïve.

00:13:37.875 --> 00:13:41.958
We thought things could maybe
end like this, uneventfully.

00:13:41.958 --> 00:13:44.625
They had everything in place.

00:13:44.625 --> 00:13:49.875
Without our knowing...
down to the tiniest, most horrible detail!

00:13:49.875 --> 00:13:54.042
These measures serve to confine
one specific dangerous creature

00:13:54.042 --> 00:13:56.000
who would do us harm.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.708
This creature, now with no place to run
thanks to the Shield of Earth,

00:13:59.708 --> 00:14:04.000
is the culprit behind
the moon's destruction one year ago.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.250
We have only found out today
that this creature--

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.125
no, this monster--

00:14:11.125 --> 00:14:14.042
is in a standoff against
the entire planet, of all things,

00:14:14.042 --> 00:14:17.000
and has taken some of our nation's
junior-high students hostage,

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.708
having gone undercover as a teacher.

00:14:20.708 --> 00:14:22.125
He is an extremely--

00:14:22.125 --> 00:14:23.333
What's going on?

00:14:23.333 --> 00:14:24.458
Looks bad!

00:14:24.458 --> 00:14:29.500
This road is closed!
Please follow our instructions!

00:14:30.125 --> 00:14:33.667
It'll take another week
for the second shot to charge up.

00:14:33.667 --> 00:14:36.417
We may have hurt our chances,
firing the first one at 20 percent

00:14:36.417 --> 00:14:38.875
just so he wouldn't see it coming.

00:14:38.875 --> 00:14:43.292
But the next one will fire
at 100 percent, and he can't get away.

00:14:43.292 --> 00:14:45.750
His death is a done deal.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:50.458
All we have to do now is manage
any fallout and deal with any troublemakers.

00:14:52.542 --> 00:14:54.125
Nagisa!

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:54.917
Kayano!

00:14:54.917 --> 00:14:57.250
What <i>is </i>all this?!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.208
Hey!

00:14:58.208 --> 00:15:00.458
Whaddya mean, "no trespassing"?!

00:15:00.458 --> 00:15:02.292
Look, just back off!

00:15:02.292 --> 00:15:03.750
Nagisa! Kayano!

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.042
Did you see the news? This is awful!

00:15:07.042 --> 00:15:08.125
Look at this!

00:15:08.125 --> 00:15:11.083
Could these be the students
that had been threatened

00:15:11.083 --> 00:15:12.458
by that monstrous teacher?

00:15:12.458 --> 00:15:14.333
--You're those junior-high hostages, right?

00:15:14.333 --> 00:15:15.583
--Excuse me! How do you feel right now?
--You're those junior-high hostages, right?

00:15:15.583 --> 00:15:18.125
--Excuse me! How do you feel right now?
--You must be relieved to hear he's been captured!

00:15:18.125 --> 00:15:20.500
Koro Sensei's been captured?

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:20.583
What was it like spending a whole year ruled by a teacher

00:15:20.583 --> 00:15:22.542
"Dangerous Creature Captured" "A Year of Fear: Students Scarred"
What was it like spending a whole year ruled by a teacher

00:15:22.542 --> 00:15:23.250
--who could explode at any second?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.167
--What's this about him forcing you to perform sham assassinations?
--who could explode at any second?

00:15:26.167 --> 00:15:27.250
--What's this about him forcing you to perform sham assassinations?
--Shut up!

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.333
It's none of your business!

00:15:29.333 --> 00:15:31.375
We have it on good authority

00:15:31.375 --> 00:15:34.708
that there's less than a 1-percent chance
of the earth being destroyed!

00:15:34.708 --> 00:15:37.292
He's not dangerous--put <i>that </i>on TV!

00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:41.000
He's not the evil teacher they're saying he is!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.125
Oh!

00:15:42.125 --> 00:15:43.667
Here, get this girl!

00:15:43.667 --> 00:15:46.667
Did that monster tell you to say that?

00:15:46.667 --> 00:15:50.958
How awful it must have been.
You can tell us the truth.

00:15:50.958 --> 00:15:55.333
<i>These </i>are the innocent children
that monster used as hostages!

00:15:55.333 --> 00:15:59.000
The children will surely
be seriously traumatized.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.125
One would hope they'll be treated as soon as possible.

00:16:01.125 --> 00:16:01.417
"Junior-High Hostages: Psychological Impact Feared"
One would hope they'll be treated as soon as possible.

00:16:01.417 --> 00:16:02.875
"Junior-High Hostages: Psychological Impact Feared"
Poor dears...

00:16:02.875 --> 00:16:08.958
"Junior-High Hostages: Psychological Impact Feared"
Who would do such terrible things to such innocent children?

00:16:08.958 --> 00:16:12.958
Why are they pitying us?

00:16:12.958 --> 00:16:16.292
You have no permission
to film here. Leave at once!

00:16:16.292 --> 00:16:19.542
B-But what about our duty to report the truth?

00:16:19.542 --> 00:16:22.083
And terrify junior-high students
for sheer entertainment value?

00:16:22.083 --> 00:16:24.042
Some duty!

00:16:24.042 --> 00:16:28.792
By the authority of the Defense Agency,
this area is off-limits.

00:16:28.792 --> 00:16:32.042
In the interest of public safety,
I'll ask you to leave.

00:16:32.042 --> 00:16:35.583
I'll take these students
into protective custody.

00:16:37.667 --> 00:16:41.792
Mr. Karasuma...
what happened to Koro Sensei?

00:16:41.792 --> 00:16:43.667
Time was up.

00:16:43.667 --> 00:16:45.958
The government implemented their last resort,

00:16:45.958 --> 00:16:48.417
the one they'd been preparing all this time.

00:16:48.417 --> 00:16:50.000
Their last resort?

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
That barrier, you mean?

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:55.583
That's only a cage to keep him trapped.

00:16:55.583 --> 00:17:00.083
In a week, they'll use
a high-power laser to kill him.

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:03.542
No! What about <i>our </i>assassination?

00:17:03.542 --> 00:17:08.417
You tried your best so far.
Now leave the rest to us.

00:17:08.417 --> 00:17:10.958
Oh, <i>now </i>you're the big man,
all "Leave it to us"?!

00:17:10.958 --> 00:17:13.583
We're completely in the dark!

00:17:13.583 --> 00:17:17.917
And that statement made it sound
like it's all Koro Sensei's fault!

00:17:17.917 --> 00:17:19.458
This is <i>not cool</i>.

00:17:19.458 --> 00:17:23.042
They told us to kill him,
and now they're elbowing in on <i>our </i>job?!

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:27.292
And it won't sit well with
Koro Sensei unless <i>we </i>do the deed!

00:17:27.292 --> 00:17:31.333
Mr. Karasuma, please--let us go!

00:17:31.333 --> 00:17:36.167
There are elite troops posted
throughout town and on the mountain.

00:17:36.167 --> 00:17:38.917
No more openings for you
to use to your advantage.

00:17:38.917 --> 00:17:40.000
Give it up.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.333
No!

00:17:41.333 --> 00:17:44.042
There's so much we haven't
talked about with Koro Sensei!

00:17:44.042 --> 00:17:46.417
So much we still want to do!

00:17:46.417 --> 00:17:48.792
So please, let us g--

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:56.375
I <i>can't </i>let you go! This is national policy!

00:17:57.375 --> 00:18:01.125
Now you listen closely, Nagisa...

00:18:01.125 --> 00:18:04.417
Don't give me a hard time.

00:18:04.417 --> 00:18:06.417
Are we clear?

00:18:07.708 --> 00:18:09.542
It's no use, Nagisa.

00:18:09.542 --> 00:18:13.250
In the end, he's just another company man.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:18.000
When push comes to shove,
he'll just follow orders to save his own skin.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.708
That's exactly right.

00:18:19.708 --> 00:18:23.542
My position lets me protect people
when they need it most.

00:18:23.542 --> 00:18:26.958
Besides, even going by my own conviction,

00:18:26.958 --> 00:18:30.292
I'm thinking he <i>should </i>be killed after all.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:36.417
Arrange transportation
and escorts for them at once.

00:18:36.417 --> 00:18:37.833
Sir!

00:18:40.833 --> 00:18:43.833
Dammit! Karasuma, that bastard!

00:18:43.833 --> 00:18:45.375
Terasaka...

00:18:45.375 --> 00:18:46.417
Huh?

00:18:46.417 --> 00:18:51.542
Mr. Karasuma just said
"Don't give me a hard time"--very clearly.

00:18:51.542 --> 00:18:53.667
Yeah? So what?

00:18:53.667 --> 00:18:57.458
Remember what he said earlier?

00:18:57.458 --> 00:19:01.542
If I ever have a hard time,
I'd trust you without hesitation.

00:19:01.542 --> 00:19:03.708
I can count on you.

00:19:03.708 --> 00:19:06.000
So I think "don't give me a hard time"

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:10.625
means he trusts us and
can count on us to handle things.

00:19:10.625 --> 00:19:16.417
We have Mr. Karasuma's trust--
he's leaving this to us. So...

00:19:16.417 --> 00:19:19.500
Let's put our heads together
and sort it all out:

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:24.625
what we want to accomplish,
what we're capable of,

00:19:24.625 --> 00:19:29.000
what Koro Sensei would want us to do.

00:19:32.917 --> 00:19:34.292
Buff buff buff buff buff!

00:19:34.292 --> 00:19:37.458
Buff it up nice, no wax needed!

00:19:39.292 --> 00:19:42.458
Ah, that's care well taken!

00:19:44.417 --> 00:19:47.750
There can't possibly be anything
for a super-creature like me to fear

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.125
this late in the game.

00:19:52.583 --> 00:19:56.000
But if I could have one wish...

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:04.375
I'd like to see them one last time.

